WEBVTT

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:03.730
Honda Ko is under our control.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.230
Wh-What did you say, Hiruma-san?

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.510
Dr. Honda.

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:13.530
The one who created Hizamaru Akari.

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:14.660
Impossible!

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:19.870
I was told Dr. Honda was killed twenty years ago.

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:23.250
I just spoke with him.

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:25.420
He seemed like he was doing fine.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.800
Th-That's wonderful.

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:36.440
His talents and his research 
weren't lost to us after all!

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:41.060
Let us invite him to U-NASA,

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:47.810
and work with him together toward 
our goal of saving humanity!

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:50.730
No.

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:55.790
My nation's technology is already 
at a level where it can

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:58.320
make proper use of Dr. Honda's research.

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:03.350
I promise we will be able to use it 
for the maximum benefit of humanity.

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:05.790
But you once...

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:07.790
Trust me.

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:51.650
<i>Shokichi seemed to have been defeated 
by No. 4 Division's hidden powers.</i>

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:54.730
<i>But they were saved from 
disaster by No. 3 Division,</i>

00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:58.460
<i>who had been supposedly working with No. 4.</i>

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:01.030
<i>Liu and Asimov...</i>

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:03.200
<i>The battle between the two</i>

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.660
<i>of them heats up as they each 
fight for what they believe in.</i>

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:27.930
Did you think we were all just engineers 
who needed weapons to fight?

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:32.900
What's wrong?

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:34.610
There are fewer of you!

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:42.120
We're fine here.

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:46.100
Bao-kun, Borgijin-kun, take 
Hong-chan into Annex I.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:47.740
Yes, General Liu.

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:51.330
Let's go.

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:53.250
Okay!

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:55.540
Wait for me, Dorjiberke-san!

00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:00.340
If you don't want an alliance, 
can you at least stay neutral?

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:59.330
Three-way

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:04.580
Your jokes are always the worst.

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:12.770
I saw that ridiculous scribbling.

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:16.610
We may not be in a position to talk,

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:20.720
but they betrayed us in a way that 
was wilder than anticipated.

00:04:21.830 --> 00:04:24.550
If they made an enemy out 
of every other division,

00:04:24.550 --> 00:04:26.740
they must have a lot of 
confidence in themselves.

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:28.850
So, Asimov-dono,

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:31.080
how did it go in the pyramids?

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:34.040
Yes, we found it.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:35.210
Good.

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:38.250
That puts us ahead, for the moment.

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:41.040
Japan has a powerful card in their hands now,

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:44.010
but that just means we need 
to reconsider our alliances.

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:46.730
Then we just follow the plan.

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:47.850
Yes.

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:51.620
We'll do all we can to create a vaccine.

00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:57.120
So is this the famous Hakkei?

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:59.520
I've never felt it before.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:03.170
I could feel the insides 
of my stomach shaking.

00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:05.400
It seemed to work on me, but...

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:10.710
Do Kung Fu masters really 
spend decades learning that?

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:15.370
The only things a real man needs are a 
full-power punch and a full-body slam!

00:05:22.140 --> 00:05:24.050
<i>A-Are you kidding me?</i>

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:27.970
<i>The man basically took a solid 
punch to his internal organs!</i>

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:32.530
Gotcha!

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:34.830
I won't let you go this time.

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:37.060
I'll take my time killing you with poison.

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:38.560
Sorry.

00:05:43.830 --> 00:05:46.730
But I've decided to cut ties with you.

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:49.200
And now I'm going to cut your torso in half!

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:52.160
I bet you can't recover from that!

00:05:56.430 --> 00:05:58.160
<i>This damn crab-man...</i>

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:01.500
<i>The best I can hope for 
here is that we both die.</i>

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:04.110
<i>Give it up! You're a soldier, right?</i>

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:07.510
Captain!

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:09.300
He's fine, Ivan.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:10.510
Don't forget your mission.

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:15.890
Now that he's like this, he'll never fall.

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:19.100
If you insist on going to help him...

00:06:21.070 --> 00:06:23.980
You'll have to kill us all first.

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:25.110
Idiots.

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:28.220
<i>Are they really intending 
to die in order to stop us?</i>

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:29.990
<i>Or are they waiting for something—</i>

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:35.290
Hey, octopus man.

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:39.580
Cut off the the poison and let the boss go.

00:06:39.580 --> 00:06:42.540
Nobody else gets to use their powers, either.

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:48.970
Otherwise I'll fire this missile I found.

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:54.220
A surface to surface missile and a launcher, 
loaded inside an exploratory vehicle.

00:06:54.220 --> 00:07:00.190
I'm amazed you managed to fit all that 
in the limited cargo space of the Annex.

00:07:00.570 --> 00:07:04.930
But the core of your plan wasn't 
this missile, or any other weapon.

00:07:04.930 --> 00:07:07.150
It's that broadcast tower.

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:11.770
Mr. Super Antenna over there's what's 
causing the communications disruption.

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:14.120
What happens if he goes down?

00:07:15.340 --> 00:07:17.610
If we can talk to Earth, 
and tell them about all the

00:07:17.610 --> 00:07:19.220
nasty little things you've been doing,

00:07:19.220 --> 00:07:22.330
your bosses back home will disavow 
you so fast your head will spin.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:26.050
"This was all their idea, not ours."

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:29.040
I'm sure your deaths will be quite painful.

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:31.510
Same for your families.

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:39.890
General Liu turned off the poison.

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:43.440
So I'll take off my mask 
and won't use my powers.

00:07:43.640 --> 00:07:45.600
Keep talking.

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:49.190
If you're blabbing like that it's 
because you want to negotiate, right?

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:54.020
We went in on your Plan Delta before,

00:07:54.020 --> 00:07:57.830
and now we want exclusive 
rights to Annex 1's lab.

00:08:08.990 --> 00:08:12.260
So, here's the story. We're not assholes.

00:08:12.850 --> 00:08:15.770
If you agree to work for us,

00:08:15.770 --> 00:08:19.680
and give up on stealing XO 
Davis and the other guy,

00:08:19.680 --> 00:08:22.650
we'll leave the tower up.

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:24.900
And we'll come up with 
something to tell Earth.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:32.550
Stop!

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:39.410
What are you thinking?

00:08:39.410 --> 00:08:42.540
Now's not the time for a honey trap.

00:08:58.900 --> 00:09:00.470
So we're back to where we started, huh?

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:02.310
Looks like the poison's bugging you, though.

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:03.520
You, too.

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:08.940
You're going to wish you 
hadn't interrupted us.

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:10.320
Xi, kill him!

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:12.230
Sure thing!

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:44.030
What's going on?

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:46.310
It's dark.

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:49.080
The sky was bright just a second ago.

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:08.910
This timing...?

00:10:11.260 --> 00:10:12.650
Was this planned?

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:22.430
They're too damn loud.

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:25.880
Are they laughing?

00:10:25.880 --> 00:10:27.180
What, Aaron?

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:29.350
They're laughing!

00:10:30.310 --> 00:10:35.020
They're laughing at us for killing each 
other, even though we're the same species!

00:10:36.090 --> 00:10:37.620
Shut the hell up!

00:10:43.530 --> 00:10:44.790
<i>They're not coming down?</i>

00:10:57.380 --> 00:10:58.640
Michelle-san!

00:11:04.100 --> 00:11:06.910
They're heading for the Annex.

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:10.060
The captain and the others...

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:11.670
What do we do?

00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:31.080
They were acting like scouts.

00:11:31.820 --> 00:11:34.520
Is their chain of command back online?

00:11:35.140 --> 00:11:39.030
We will meet up with No. 
6 Division as planned.

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:39.970
Roger.

00:11:45.100 --> 00:11:47.100
<i>They have a leader.</i>

00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:56.640
<i>Is that him?</i>

00:12:03.010 --> 00:12:05.140
Is that a dragonfly?

00:12:05.470 --> 00:12:06.420
A dragonfly?

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:08.260
No doubt about it.

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:10.700
It's a terraformar with dragonfly wings.

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:12.940
An oniyanma.

00:12:12.940 --> 00:12:14.170
Is that bad?

00:12:14.170 --> 00:12:15.330
It's fast.

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:16.970
The only one who could keep up with it is...

00:12:21.610 --> 00:12:23.550
It's floating? Seriously?

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:24.800
Take this!

00:12:41.970 --> 00:12:42.780
Aaron!

00:12:50.550 --> 00:12:52.660
Aaron! Aaron!

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:16.150
<i>No! They took the bodies!</i>

00:13:37.950 --> 00:13:39.250
Children?

00:13:39.530 --> 00:13:41.910
<i>We expected that they'd have children.</i>

00:13:41.910 --> 00:13:43.710
<i>But why only send children?</i>

00:13:44.030 --> 00:13:46.870
<i>They had a highly talented leader.</i>

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:52.790
<i>They relied too much on it, and that's 
why they didn't attack until now.</i>

00:13:53.460 --> 00:13:57.790
<i>And they recovered from it in just a week?</i>

00:14:30.630 --> 00:14:31.970
Xi-san,

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:35.210
get inside and tell Hong-chan to hurry.

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:46.280
Okay, don't come inside, please!

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:48.240
Right. Hurry it up.

00:14:50.120 --> 00:14:52.510
I mean it, okay?

00:14:56.550 --> 00:14:59.350
We need to hurry and get enough for everyone.

00:14:59.350 --> 00:15:01.880
I don't know what's going on, but it seems 
like there's a lot of noise outside.

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:15.970
<b>Oniyanma Dragonfly Terraformar:
Possesses a compound eye with 28,000 eyes, 
the largest number of any insect, and also is highly maneuverable.  
It's capable of quick takeoffs, quick stops, backwards flight, circling, 
and hovering, movements which man-made vehicles like helicopters 
and airplanes cannot replicate. Oniyanma Dragonflies tend to chase
 anything that flaps its wings, and in battles with other insects they are essentially invincible.</b>

00:15:20.790 --> 00:15:21.780
<i>They're fast!</i>

00:15:25.110 --> 00:15:26.920
Damn you!

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:29.610
<i>No! The captain!</i>

00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:31.240
<i>Why, you...</i>

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:33.170
<i>He's only regenerated his left arm,</i>

00:15:33.170 --> 00:15:34.570
<i>and the poison...</i>

00:15:42.570 --> 00:15:44.600
<i>They're not all attacking at once?</i>

00:15:44.600 --> 00:15:45.920
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:49.920
<i>That dragonfly's just working 
on splitting us apart.</i>

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:51.220
It's toying with us!

00:15:51.220 --> 00:15:53.180
<i>No, it's not.</i>

00:15:53.740 --> 00:15:54.900
<i>It's the opposite.</i>

00:15:56.630 --> 00:15:58.520
<i>It's teaching them!</i>

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:16.480
Take this!

00:16:16.520 --> 00:16:17.820
Shithead!

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:26.700
So I'm just your training tool, assholes?

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:30.960
<i>They're not just relying on their boss.</i>

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:34.090
<i>They all want to learn?</i>

00:16:39.390 --> 00:16:40.440
Nina!

00:16:53.700 --> 00:16:54.530
Oh, no!

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:08.220
Don't stop moving.

00:17:08.690 --> 00:17:11.590
Sanjo-san, full speed!

00:17:18.810 --> 00:17:20.220
Ivan!

00:17:21.060 --> 00:17:22.230
I know!

00:17:23.200 --> 00:17:26.100
My mission is to keep the wounded safe

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:28.900
and, if I have to, escape myself!

00:17:34.050 --> 00:17:36.900
Captain, hold your breath, please.

00:17:50.070 --> 00:17:53.640
<i>Oniyanmas tend to follow 
things that flap their wings.</i>

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:55.320
<i>I knew it would come after me.</i>

00:17:55.810 --> 00:17:57.050
<i>The problem is...</i>

00:18:03.010 --> 00:18:05.430
Your coach left you.

00:18:19.880 --> 00:18:23.620
Maybe they've evolved and learned 
to let their guard down.

00:18:24.130 --> 00:18:26.290
They're trying to let their second-stringers

00:18:26.290 --> 00:18:29.080
get some experience by 
fighting a weaker team, huh?

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:31.970
Well, that might be the case.

00:18:31.970 --> 00:18:35.280
But the 5000 or so full-grown bugs above us

00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:37.020
probably aren't after us.

00:18:38.570 --> 00:18:40.730
They're after the Annex itself.

00:18:50.510 --> 00:18:51.860
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:18:59.040 --> 00:19:00.700
<i>They are bugs, after all!</i>

00:19:01.250 --> 00:19:04.280
<i>Not one of them is afraid of death!</i>

00:19:09.510 --> 00:19:11.540
<i>This is disgusting!</i>

00:19:21.230 --> 00:19:22.550
<i>Ivan's poison...</i>

00:19:23.020 --> 00:19:25.260
<i>But it's about to stop working,</i>

00:19:25.260 --> 00:19:27.680
<i>so now I have to run as fast as I can!</i>

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:37.130
<i>It's not following me?</i>

00:19:45.590 --> 00:19:48.020
Captain, this is the only 
moment we have to act.

00:19:48.020 --> 00:19:49.830
If we run away now,

00:19:50.360 --> 00:19:55.380
then several others will 
be able to survive, as well.

00:19:55.960 --> 00:20:00.030
We'll lose the Annex to the cockroaches, 
but we won't lose it to the No. 4 Division.

00:20:30.770 --> 00:20:31.870
What is that?

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:41.220
The Full Danger Zone Rescue and Combat 
Armor Suit, "Man in the Shell".

00:20:45.780 --> 00:20:51.610
I told you, if you plan to 
fight humans, you can't win!

00:20:52.690 --> 00:20:55.070
No matter how unethical we have to get,

00:20:55.070 --> 00:20:57.050
we won't let you have the Annex!

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:05.500
Everyone, get out of here!

00:21:05.500 --> 00:21:07.010
That's a bacteria type!

00:21:31.380 --> 00:21:32.770
<i>Just wait for me.</i>

00:21:33.310 --> 00:21:36.130
<i>I'll make a vaccine and bring it back!</i>

00:21:44.620 --> 00:21:45.850
<i>Gina!</i>

00:22:01.570 --> 00:22:04.450
M.A.R.S. Ranking #7
Alexander Asimov
Surgery Base:
Dorcus Titanus Sumatra

00:23:36.050 --> 00:23:41.020
Soldier and Father

00:23:36.910 --> 00:23:40.480
I just want to protect my family!
